# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Node / Vite
web/node_modules/

# Cached BGG API responses (regenerated on demand)
data/cache/

# The live capture is generated by `python -m pipeline.fetch`; only the seed
# proxy dataset (data/games.seed.json) is committed.
data/games.json

# BGG's ranks dump — 11 MB, and BGG regenerates it regularly, so a committed
# copy would go stale in the history. `pipeline.fetch` needs it and raises an
# error naming the download page (boardgamegeek.com/data_dumps/bg_ranks) when
# it's absent. See README, "Refresh from live BoardGameGeek data".
data/boardgames_ranks.csv

# The built site (docs/) and web/public/grid.json ARE committed on purpose:
# GitHub Pages serves docs/, and the grid JSON is the reviewable output.
